From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] staging: ion: demote restartable share pool wait log

The share-pool monitor ioctl uses wait_event_interruptible().  A benign
signal such as SIGCHLD can therefore return -ERESTARTSYS before userspace
retries the ioctl.  The X5 hbmem fork-process sample reliably exercises
this path when its diagnostic system() calls reap child processes, causing
two misleading info-level "failed -512" messages despite successful pool
operation and cleanup.

Keep the return value and retry semantics unchanged.  Log the expected
restartable interruption at debug level while retaining info-level logging
for all other failures.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 drivers/staging/android/ion/ion.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/android/ion/ion.c b/drivers/staging/android/ion/ion.c
index 000000000..000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/android/ion/ion.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/android/ion/ion.c
@@ -4383,7 +4383,10 @@ static int32_t ion_share_pool_monitor_ref_cnt(struct ion_client *client,
 	//coverity[misra_c_2012_rule_20_7_violation:SUPPRESS], ## violation reason SYSSW_V_20.7_01
 	ret = (int32_t) wait_event_interruptible(client->wq, client->wq_cnt != 0);
 	if (ret != 0) {
-		(void)pr_info("%s failed %d\n", __func__, ret);
+		if (ret == -ERESTARTSYS)
+			pr_debug("%s interrupted %d\n", __func__, ret);
+		else
+			(void)pr_info("%s failed %d\n", __func__, ret);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
